Welcome to Termux!

Docs:       https://termux.dev/docs
Donate:     https://termux.dev/donate
Community:  https://termux.dev/community

Working with Termux packages (apt/dpkg):

 - Search:  pkg search <query>
 - Install: pkg install <package>
 - Update:  pkg update
 - Upgrade: pkg upgrade

Working with Nix (native build, no proot):

 - Version: nix --version
 - Eval:    nix eval --expr '1 + 2'
 - Query:   nix-env -q
 - Help:    nix-env --help

Note: stock nixpkgs packages cannot bootstrap on Android, so nix-env is
useful for self-contained derivations and Nix store paths, not for
installing arbitrary nixpkgs packages. See the Nix source tree's
packaging/termux/README.md for details.

Notes:

 - The Nix store lives at $PREFIX/nix/store; state and the DB under
   $PREFIX/var/nix; per-user profiles under ~/.local/state/nix;
   configuration in $PREFIX/etc/nix/nix.conf.
 - Android has no user namespaces and SELinux blocks chroot/mount, so Nix
   builds always run unsandboxed. This is an Android limitation.
 - Stock nixpkgs cannot bootstrap on Android; self-contained derivations do
   build. See packaging/termux/README.md in the Nix source tree.
